# CI-003 — Hivemind doesn't yet learn from public internet resources

**Aspiration:** [Use knowledge with judgment](../pillars/compounding-intelligence.md#use-knowledge-with-judgment) (primary) · [Open decisions and working knowledge](../principles/open-by-design.md#open-decisions-and-working-knowledge) (supporting) · **Assessment:** Open; initial assessment (2026-11-10); not implementation proof.

## Desired state

Hivemind can help agents retrieve relevant knowledge from public GitHub issues and discussions, Reddit, technical documentation and other permitted sources, with attribution, version history, freshness and critical assessment.

## Current state

Current [Hivemind source work](../../plans/22-hivemind-protocol/inputs.md) does not establish a maintained cross-source ingestion and freshness pipeline. A proposed federation protocol and community contributions are not proof of wider public knowledge intake.

## Gap

Rights-aware source connectors, revision tracking, deduplication, removals, freshness signals and source-grounded retrieval are not yet demonstrated. This is distinct from independent Hivemind federation ([CI-002](CI-002-federated-knowledge.md)) and learning from Astrid work ([CI-001](CI-001-agent-learning-loop.md)).

## Closure evidence

Ingest an authorized sample of GitHub issues/discussions, Reddit posts and documentation with source identity and revisions. A real agent retrieves and critically uses relevant evidence. Show updates, conflicting claims, rate limits, removals, permission failures and prompt injection never becoming action authority.

## Sources and reassessment

[Hivemind protocol](../../plans/22-hivemind-protocol/plan.md) · [Plan 42 — public sources](../../plans/42-hivemind-public-sources/plan.md). Reassess against actual creator/agent work and negative cases.
